  "section_notes": "S2 sets a 7% permanent failure ceiling (not 5%) with per-model rates given to purchasers but not published, which keeps Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%) on sale. S5 has no mandatory recall: corrective action can replace recall indefinitely, which protects Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9 per 100k). S1 is strong (24-hour reporting of all incidents, including unconfirmed ones), which constrains both companies' unreported incidents."
